course: dictionary
lesson: 10516
title: One word, many meanings: two
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Two usually means the number 2, one more than one. Context tells you which meaning you need. «Two tough recorders called the black box help investigators» means two real objects, so two is a number here.
explain: Some uses do not count anything. In «in two», two means in two pieces, and in «two-faced», it means saying one thing and doing another. Ask what would fit in the sentence. If "in two pieces" makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: Texts and exams use two in different ways. In a text, «me 2» means «me too», and the 2 is a short way of writing to or too. In exams, formal words such as twofold, both, double or a pair of can replace two. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Two is the number 2, one more than one.
fact: A two can be the digit 2, or a card or dice face showing 2.
fact: «In two» means in two pieces.
fact: «Me 2» is casual texting for «me too».
fact: A couple often means two, but it can also mean a few.
fact: Formal words for two include twofold, both, double, duplicate and a pair of.
exercise: «Two tough recorders called the black box help investigators find out why.» How many recorders are there? | Ten | *Two | Three | One
exercise: Ayla texts «me 2». What does the 2 mean? | Two pieces | Second place | *Me too | The number two, one more than one
exercise: «The cake was split in two.» What does in two mean? | Eaten all at once | *In two pieces | Hidden under a plate
test: «Some pictures, like the duck-rabbit, can be seen in two ways.» What does two ways mean here? | Two very large ways | Two ways to fly | *Two different ways of seeing
test: Which of these is NOT a formal word for two? | *Twelve | Both | Twofold | Duplicate
exam: In «The Zebra and the Giraffe count "One--two--three!"», what is two? | A casual text word meaning too | A playing card | *A number in a count | A pair of animals
